      "kind": "stocktake_settlement",
      "classification": "deliberate_difference",
      "reason": "The stocktake is built (WP27). Approving a count here posts one journal of its own, dated the day of the approval, that holds the loss of the item that is short and the gain of the item that is over at the current average of the location, and it makes no stock permit; the reference system makes two automatic permits, one in and one out, each with a journal of its own. The amounts on the stock and cost of sales accounts are the same, the number of documents and journals is not. The executive decision taken under E47 (E111) is one journal and not two automatic permits, and the owner can overturn it.",
      "reference_decimals": 2,
      "evidence": [
        "stocktake_settlement"
      ],
